{"title": "Quant Super Practice — Mock #11", "duration_min": 20.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>A merchant bought two watches for &#8377;9,000 each. He sold one watch at a loss of 10%. At what price (in &#8377;) should he sell the other watch to earn a profit of 18% overall?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; 9,000 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368;&#2306;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; 10% &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368;&#2404; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; 18% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; (&#8377; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["14,130", "14,310", "13,140", "13,410"], "options_hi": ["14,130", "14,310", "13,140", "13,410"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Total cost price = 2*9000 = &#8377;18000</p><p>Overall selling price = 118% of 18000 = &#8377;21240</p><p>Selling price of one watch = 90% of 9000 = &#8377;8100</p><p>Selling price of other watch = 21240 - 8100 = &#8377;13140</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total cost price = 2*9000 = &#8377;18000</p><p>Overall selling price = 118% of 18000 = &#8377;21240</p><p>Selling price of one watch = 90% of 9000 = &#8377;8100</p><p>Selling price of other watch = 21240 - 8100 = &#8377;13140</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>If the market price of a bag is 25% above the cost price, and a discount of 18% is declared on it, then find the gain percentage.</p>", "q_hi": "&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2348;&#2376;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2348;&#2366;&#2332;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351;, &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; 25% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2313;&#2360; &#2346;&#2352; 18% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2328;&#2379;&#2359;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;", "options_en": ["1.5%", "2.0%", "3.0%", "2.5%"], "options_hi": ["1.5%", "2.0%", "3.0%", "2.5%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the cost price = Rs. 100</p><p>Marked price = 100 * 125/100 = Rs. 125</p><p>Selling price = 125 * 82/100 = Rs. 102.5</p><p>Gain percentage = (102.5  -  100)/100 * 100 = 2.5%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the cost price = Rs. 100</p><p>Marked price = 100 * 125/100 = Rs. 125</p><p>Selling price = 125 * 82/100 = Rs. 102.5</p><p>Gain percentage = (102.5  -  100)/100 * 100 = 2.5%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A seller offers a discount of 12% if the total sale price of different products purchased by a single customer is below &#8377;3,000, and discount of 15% if the total sale value of all the products exceeds &#8377;3,000. A shirt costing &#8377;900 was sold to Anand after earning a margin of 9% and also a jacket costing &#8377;1,900 was sold to him after a margin of 6%. How much does Anand have to pay (in &#8377;) for the final settlement of the bill?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2348;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; 3,000 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; 12% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2348;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; 3,000 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; 15% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 900 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2358;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2310;&#2344;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2379; 9% &#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2344; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; 1,900 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2332;&#2376;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2349;&#2368; 6% &#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2344; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312;&#2404; &#2348;&#2367;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2344;&#2367;&#2346;&#2335;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2310;&#2344;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; (&#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["2,953.60", "3,005.40", "2,645.60", "2,635.60"], "options_hi": ["2,953.60", "3,005.40", "2,645.60", "2,635.60"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Cost price of shirt = &#8377;900</p><p>Selling price of shirt = 109% of 900 = 981</p><p>Cost price of jacket = &#8377;1900</p><p>Selling price of jacket = 106% of 1900 = 2014</p><p>Total selling price = 981 + 2014 = &#8377;2995</p><p>Since 2995 &lt; 3000</p><p>Discounted price at 12% = (100  -  12)% of 2995 = &#8377;2635.6</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Cost price of shirt = &#8377;900</p><p>Selling price of shirt = 109% of 900 = 981</p><p>Cost price of jacket = &#8377;1900</p><p>Selling price of jacket = 106% of 1900 = 2014</p><p>Total selling price = 981 + 2014 = &#8377;2995</p><p>Since 2995 &lt; 3000</p><p>Discounted price at 12% = (100  -  12)% of 2995 = &#8377;2635.6</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>On the occasion of Republic Day, a retail store offers a scheme where customers can avail a discount of 26% on their total purchase. If Manish buys items worth &#8377; 2,050, how much money (in &#8377;) will he save through the scheme discount</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2327;&#2339;&#2340;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2357;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2357;&#2360;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2369;&#2342;&#2352;&#2366; &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2379;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2361;&#2340; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342; &#2346;&#2352; 26% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2313;&#2336;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2350;&#2344;&#2368;&#2359; 2,050 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2319;&#2305; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2361; &#2311;&#2360; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2350; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2376;&#2360;&#2375; (&#8377; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2348;&#2330;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;</p>", "options_en": ["533", "544", "522", "511"], "options_hi": ["533", "544", "522", "511"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Discount = 26% of 2050</p><p>= 0.26  X  2050</p><p>= 0.26  X  (2000 + 50)</p><p>= (0.26  X  2000) + (0.26  X  50)</p><p>= 520 + 13 = 533</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Discount = 26% of 2050</p><p>= 0.26  X  2050</p><p>= 0.26  X  (2000 + 50)</p><p>= (0.26  X  2000) + (0.26  X  50)</p><p>= 520 + 13 = 533</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Rohini buys a Bluetooth headphone set for &#8377;1,700 from a wholesale shop and marks it at &#8377;2,000. Later on, she allows a discount of 40% on its sale. What is her loss or gain percentage (correct up to two decimal places)?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2352;&#2379;&#2361;&#2367;&#2339;&#2368; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2341;&#2379;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375; 1,700 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2381;&#2354;&#2370;&#2335;&#2370;&#2341; &#2361;&#2375;&#2337;&#2347;&#2379;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375;&#2335; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; 2,000 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2348;&#2340;&#2366;&#2312;&#2404; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2357;&#2361; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; 40% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; (&#2342;&#2379; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368;)?", "options_en": ["25.19% loss", "29.41% gain", "29.41% loss", "25.19% gain"], "options_hi": ["25.19% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;", "29.41% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;", "29.41% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;", "25.19% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Selling price = 2000 * 60/100 = Rs. 1200</p><p>Loss percentage = (1700  -  1200)/1700 * 100 = 29.41%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Selling price = 2000 * 60/100 = Rs. 1200</p><p>Loss percentage = (1700  -  1200)/1700 * 100 = 29.41%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Raman fixes the sale price of his goods at 16% above the cost price. He sells his goods at 12% less than the fixed price. Find the profit percentage correct to two places of decimal.</p>", "q_hi": "&#2352;&#2350;&#2344; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; 16% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; 12% &#2325;&#2350; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;", "options_en": ["1.07%", "2.08%", "0.08%", "3.01%"], "options_hi": ["1.07%", "2.08%", "0.08%", "3.01%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Assume the cost price is 100.</p><p>Marked price = 100  X  (1 + 0.16) = 116.</p><p>Selling price = 116  X  (1 &#8722; 0.12) = 116  X  0.88 = 102.08.</p><p>Profit = 102.08 &#8722; 100 = 2.08.</p><p>Profit percentage = (2.08/100)  X  100 = 2.08%.</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Assume the cost price is 100.</p><p>Marked price = 100  X  (1 + 0.16) = 116.</p><p>Selling price = 116  X  (1 &#8722; 0.12) = 116  X  0.88 = 102.08.</p><p>Profit = 102.08 &#8722; 100 = 2.08.</p><p>Profit percentage = (2.08/100)  X  100 = 2.08%.</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A man loses 28% by selling an article for &#8377;144. If he sells it for &#8377;288, what will be his gain/loss percentage?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; 144 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; 28% &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2361; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 288 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;/&#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?", "options_en": ["Gain, 41%", "Loss, 43%", "Gain, 44%", "Loss, 46%"], "options_hi": ["&#2354;&#2366;&#2349;, 41%", "&#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;, 43%", "&#2354;&#2366;&#2349;, 44%", "&#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;, 46%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>On selling an item for Rs. 144</p><p>Loss = 28%</p><p>C.P = (144/72)*100 =Rs 200</p><p>Now, if he sells it for Rs. 288, then gain = 288  -  200 =88</p><p>Gain%= (88/200)*100 =44%</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>On selling an item for Rs. 144</p><p>Loss = 28%</p><p>C.P = (144/72)*100 =Rs 200</p><p>Now, if he sells it for Rs. 288, then gain = 288  -  200 =88</p><p>Gain%= (88/200)*100 =44%</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A vegetable vendor bought 100 kg of potatoes at the rate of &#8377;19 per kg and spent &#8377;100 as cartage. He sold 60 kg of potatoes with a 50% profit and half of the remaining stock with a 40% profit. He sold half of the still remaining potatoes with a 25% profit. What profit percentage should he aim for when selling the ultimate remaining potatoes to achieve an overall profit of 42%? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2348;&#2381;&#2332;&#2368; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; 100 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2310;&#2354;&#2370; 19 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 100 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335;&#2375;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2330; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; 60 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2310;&#2354;&#2370; 50% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2377;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; 40% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2348;&#2330;&#2375; &#2310;&#2354;&#2370; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; 25% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;&#2404; 42% &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2348;&#2330;&#2375; &#2310;&#2354;&#2370; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2381;&#2351; &#2352;&#2326;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;? </p>", "options_en": ["0.16", "0.1", "0.12", "0.15"], "options_hi": ["0.16", "0.1", "0.12", "0.15"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Total cost price = 100 * 19 + 100 = &#8377;2000 </p><p>Cost price per kg = 2000/100 = &#8377;20 </p><p>Overall selling price = 142% of 2000 = 2840</p><p>Selling price =&gt;</p><p>At 50% profit = 150% of 60 * 20 = 1800</p><p>At 40% profit = 140% of (100  -  60)/2 * 20 = 560</p><p>At 25% profit = 125% of (100  -  60)/4 * 20 = 250</p><p>At x% profit = (100 + x)% of (100  -  60)/4 * 20 = 2(100 + x)</p><p>Now, </p><p>1800 + 560 + 250 + 2(100 + x) = 2840</p><p>2810 + 2x = 2840</p><p>2x = 30</p><p>x = 15% = 0.15</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total cost price = 100 * 19 + 100 = &#8377;2000 </p><p>Cost price per kg = 2000/100 = &#8377;20 </p><p>Overall selling price = 142% of 2000 = 2840</p><p>Selling price =&gt;</p><p>At 50% profit = 150% of 60 * 20 = 1800</p><p>At 40% profit = 140% of (100  -  60)/2 * 20 = 560</p><p>At 25% profit = 125% of (100  -  60)/4 * 20 = 250</p><p>At x% profit = (100 + x)% of (100  -  60)/4 * 20 = 2(100 + x)</p><p>Now, </p><p>1800 + 560 + 250 + 2(100 + x) = 2840</p><p>2810 + 2x = 2840</p><p>2x = 30</p><p>x = 15% = 0.15</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>An article costs&#8377;1,000 for a salesman. He fixes its marked price as&#8377;1,500. He sells it to a customer at a discount of 20%. He gives a furtherdiscount of 10% for each cash payment. Find the percentage of loss or gain that the salesman makes on sale.</p>", "q_hi": "&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; 1,000 &#2352;&#2369;. &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; 1,500 &#2352;&#2369;. &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; 20% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2346;&#2352; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2344;&#2325;&#2342; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; 10% &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;", "options_en": ["Gain 8%", "gain 10%", "loss 8%", "loss 10%"], "options_hi": ["8% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;", "10% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;", "&#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; 8%", "&#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; 10%"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Marked Price Discount:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;20% discount on &#8377;1,500 gives:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Selling Price after first discount = 1500  X  0.80 = &#8377;1,200.</p><p>Further Cash Discount:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;10% discount on &#8377;1,200 gives:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Final Selling Price = 1200  X  0.90 = &#8377;1,080.</p><p>Profit Calculation:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Cost Price = &#8377;1,000</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Profit = 1080  -  1000 = &#8377;80</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Profit Percentage = (80/1000)  X  100 = 8% gain</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Marked Price Discount:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;20% discount on &#8377;1,500 gives:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Selling Price after first discount = 1500  X  0.80 = &#8377;1,200.</p><p>Further Cash Discount:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;10% discount on &#8377;1,200 gives:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Final Selling Price = 1200  X  0.90 = &#8377;1,080.</p><p>Profit Calculation:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Cost Price = &#8377;1,000</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Profit = 1080  -  1000 = &#8377;80</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Profit Percentage = (80/1000)  X  100 = 8% gain</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A man buys a machine for Rs.5,000. After one year, he sells it for Rs.6,000. After two years, again he buys the same machine at Rs.8,000 and sells it for Rs.10,000. Find his overall profit percentage for both the transactions.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; 5,000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2358;&#2368;&#2344; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2357;&#2361; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; 6,000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2357;&#2361; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2358;&#2368;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; 8,000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 10,000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2354;&#2375;&#2344;&#2342;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["20.23%", "23.08%", "18.75%", "15.23%"], "options_hi": ["20.23%", "23.08%", "18.75%", "15.23%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>First Time:</p><p>C.P = Rs.5000</p><p>S.P = Rs.6000</p><p>Profit = 6000  -  5000 = Rs.1000</p><p>Second Time:</p><p>C.P = Rs.8000</p><p>S.P = Rs.10000</p><p>Profit = 10000  -  8000 = Rs.2000</p><p>Overall profit = 2000 + 1000 = Rs.3000</p><p>Overall profit percentage = 3000/(5000 + 8000) * 100 = 23.07%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>First Time:</p><p>C.P = Rs.5000</p><p>S.P = Rs.6000</p><p>Profit = 6000  -  5000 = Rs.1000</p><p>Second Time:</p><p>C.P = Rs.8000</p><p>S.P = Rs.10000</p><p>Profit = 10000  -  8000 = Rs.2000</p><p>Overall profit = 2000 + 1000 = Rs.3000</p><p>Overall profit percentage = 3000/(5000 + 8000) * 100 = 23.07%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Murlidhar, the owner of a grocery store, offers a discount scheme 'buy 5 water bottles get 1 for free' to his customers. What is the effective percentage discount offered by Murlidhar? (correct up to two decimal places)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2379;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325; &#2350;&#2369;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2343;&#2352; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; '5 &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2379;&#2340;&#2354; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; 1 &#2350;&#2369;&#2347;&#2364;&#2381;&#2340;' &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2350;&#2369;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2343;&#2352; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2342;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;? (&#2342;&#2379; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368;)</p>", "options_en": ["13.67%", "20.00%", "13.33%", "16.67%"], "options_hi": ["13.67%", "20.00%", "13.33%", "16.67%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Buy 5 water bottles get 1 for free</p><p>Let marked price = 6</p><p>Selling price = 5</p><p>Discount = 6  -  5 = 1</p><p>Discount % = (1/6) * 100 = 16.67%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Buy 5 water bottles get 1 for free</p><p>Let marked price = 6</p><p>Selling price = 5</p><p>Discount = 6  -  5 = 1</p><p>Discount % = (1/6) * 100 = 16.67%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A doll is marked for &#8377;2,500. A customer pays &#8377;1,800 for it. If the customer got a series of two discounts and the rate of the first discount is 10%, then the rate of the second discount is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2369;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; 2,500 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 1,800 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2330;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2361;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; 10% &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;:</p>", "options_en": ["25%", "18%", "15%", "20%"], "options_hi": ["25%", "18%", "15%", "20%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let 2<sup>nd</sup> discount = d%</p><p>Marked price of doll = &#8377;2500</p><p>Selling price of doll = &#8377;1800</p><p>Now,</p><p>(100  -  10)% of (100  -  d)% of 2500 = 1800</p><p>25(100  -  d) = 2000</p><p>100  -  d = 80</p><p>d = 20%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let 2<sup>nd</sup> discount = d%</p><p>Marked price of doll = &#8377;2500</p><p>Selling price of doll = &#8377;1800</p><p>Now,</p><p>(100  -  10)% of (100  -  d)% of 2500 = 1800</p><p>25(100  -  d) = 2000</p><p>100  -  d = 80</p><p>d = 20%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A man buys 10 identical articles for a total of &#8377;15. If he sells each of them for &#8377;1.7, then his profit percentage will be _ % (rounded off to two decimal places).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2342;&#2350;&#2368; 10 &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2319;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 15 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2361; &#2313;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; 1.7 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; _ % (&#2342;&#2379; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;) &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["14.33", "12.76", "13.33", "11.76"], "options_hi": ["14.33", "12.76", "13.33", "11.76"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Cost Price (CP) Calculation:</p><p>Total cost for 10 articles = &#8377;15</p><p>Cost per article = 15 / 10 = &#8377;1.5</p><p>Selling Price (SP):</p><p>Selling price per article = &#8377;1.7</p><p>Profit per article:</p><p>Profit = SP - CP = 1.7 - 1.5 = &#8377;0.2</p><p>Profit Percentage:</p><p>Profit % = (Profit / CP)  X  100</p><p>= (0.2 / 1.5)  X  100</p><p>= (20 / 1.5) = 200 / 15 = 13.333..%</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Cost Price (CP) Calculation:</p><p>Total cost for 10 articles = &#8377;15</p><p>Cost per article = 15 / 10 = &#8377;1.5</p><p>Selling Price (SP):</p><p>Selling price per article = &#8377;1.7</p><p>Profit per article:</p><p>Profit = SP - CP = 1.7 - 1.5 = &#8377;0.2</p><p>Profit Percentage:</p><p>Profit % = (Profit / CP)  X  100</p><p>= (0.2 / 1.5)  X  100</p><p>= (20 / 1.5) = 200 / 15 = 13.333..%</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the single discount equivalent to the successive discounts of 20%, 35%, and 10%?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>20%, 35% &#2324;&#2352; 10% &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2319;&#2325;&#2354; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["53.2%", "48.7%", "65.4%", "42.3%"], "options_hi": ["53.2%", "48.7%", "65.4%", "42.3%"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Single discount equivalent to 20% and 35% = 20 + 35  -  (20 * 35)/100 = 55  -  7 = 48%</p><p>Now, single discount equivalent to 48% and 10% = 48 + 10  -  (48 * 10)/100 = 58  -  4.8 = 53.2%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Single discount equivalent to 20% and 35% = 20 + 35  -  (20 * 35)/100 = 55  -  7 = 48%</p><p>Now, single discount equivalent to 48% and 10% = 48 + 10  -  (48 * 10)/100 = 58  -  4.8 = 53.2%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Products pass successively through the hands of three traders and each of them sells his goods at a profit of 30% of his cost price. If the last trader sold the products for Rs.300, then how much did the first trader pay for them?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2375; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2379; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375; 30% &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2344;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; 300 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2344;&#2375; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.330.55 (approx.)", "Rs.136.55 (approx.)", "Rs.240.55 (approx.)", "Rs.137.55 (approx.)"], "options_hi": ["330.55 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; (&#2354;&#2327;&#2349;&#2327;)", "136.55 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; (&#2354;&#2327;&#2349;&#2327;)", "240.55 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; (&#2354;&#2327;&#2349;&#2327;)", "137.55 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; (&#2354;&#2327;&#2349;&#2327;)"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the cost price of first trader = p</p><p>p * (130/100) * (130/100) * (130/100) = 300</p><p>p = 300000/2197</p><p>p = &#8377;136.55</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the cost price of first trader = p</p><p>p * (130/100) * (130/100) * (130/100) = 300</p><p>p = 300000/2197</p><p>p = &#8377;136.55</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A bike is sold for &#8377;87,500 by allowing a discount of 44% on its marked price. The marked price (in&#8377;) of the bike is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; 44% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2375;&#2325;&#2352; &#8377; 87,500 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; (&#8377; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["1,56,100", "1,58,225", "1,56,250", "1,55,500"], "options_hi": ["1,56,100", "1,58,225", "1,56,250", "1,55,500"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let MP be Rs. x</p><p>Discount = 44% of x = 11x / 25</p><p>SP = MP - Discount</p><p>=&gt;87500 = x - 11x / 25</p><p>=&gt;14x / 25 = 87500</p><p>=&gt;x = 87500 * 25/14 = Rs. 156250</p><p>So, MP = Rs. 156250</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let MP be Rs. x</p><p>Discount = 44% of x = 11x / 25</p><p>SP = MP - Discount</p><p>=&gt;87500 = x - 11x / 25</p><p>=&gt;14x / 25 = 87500</p><p>=&gt;x = 87500 * 25/14 = Rs. 156250</p><p>So, MP = Rs. 156250</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Ramesh purchased 130 books at the rate of &#8377;200 each and sold half of them at the rate of &#8377;300 each, one-fifth of them at the rate of &#8377;350 each and the rest at the cost price. Find his profit percentage.</p>", "q_hi": "&#2352;&#2350;&#2375;&#2358; &#2344;&#2375; 130 &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377;200 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2368; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377;300 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375;, &#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330;&#2357;&#2366;&#2305; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#8377;350 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368;&#2306;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;", "options_en": ["35%", "40%", "38%", "44%"], "options_hi": ["35%", "40%", "38%", "44%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total cost price = 130 * 200 = &#8377;26000</p><p>Selling price of 65 books = 65 * 300 = &#8377;19500</p><p>Selling price of 130/5 or 26 books = 26 * 350 = &#8377;9100</p><p>Selling price of remaining 39 books = 39 * 200 = &#8377;7800</p><p>Total selling price = 19500 + 9100 + 7800 = 36400</p><p>Profit percentage = (36400  -  26000)/26000 * 100 = 40%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total cost price = 130 * 200 = &#8377;26000</p><p>Selling price of 65 books = 65 * 300 = &#8377;19500</p><p>Selling price of 130/5 or 26 books = 26 * 350 = &#8377;9100</p><p>Selling price of remaining 39 books = 39 * 200 = &#8377;7800</p><p>Total selling price = 19500 + 9100 + 7800 = 36400</p><p>Profit percentage = (36400  -  26000)/26000 * 100 = 40%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Aarav owns a watch worth &#8377;10,000. He sells it to Bhavin at a profit of 15%. After some days, Bhavin sells it back to Aarav at 15% loss. Find the percentage profit or loss faced by Aarav.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2310;&#2352;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; 10,000 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; 15% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2367;&#2344; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360; &#2310;&#2352;&#2357; &#2325;&#2379; 15% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2310;&#2352;&#2357; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;, &#2351;&#2361; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["17.25% loss", "17.25% profit", "18.25% profit", "18.75% loss"], "options_hi": ["17.25% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;", "17.25% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;", "18.25% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;", "18.75% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Cost price for Aarav = &#8377;10000</p><p>Selling price = 115% of 10000 = &#8377;11500</p><p>New cost price = 85% of 11500 = &#8377;9775</p><p>Loss percentage = [(11500  -  9775)/10000]*100 = 17.25% profit</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Cost price for Aarav = &#8377;10000</p><p>Selling price = 115% of 10000 = &#8377;11500</p><p>New cost price = 85% of 11500 = &#8377;9775</p><p>Loss percentage = [(11500  -  9775)/10000]*100 = 17.25% profit</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the gain percentage, given that Aditi sold her scooter for &#8377;40620 gaining 1/5<sup>th</sup> of the selling price.</p>", "q_hi": "&#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; &#2309;&#2342;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2335;&#2352; &le;40620 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; 1/5&#2357;&#2366;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404;", "options_en": ["10%", "20%", "25%", "35%"], "options_hi": ["10%", "20%", "25%", "35%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Selling price = &#8377;40620</p><p>Profit = 40620 * 1/5 = &#8377;8124</p><p>Cost price = 40620  -  8124 = &#8377;32496</p><p>Gain% = 8124/32496 * 100 = 25%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Selling price = &#8377;40620</p><p>Profit = 40620 * 1/5 = &#8377;8124</p><p>Cost price = 40620  -  8124 = &#8377;32496</p><p>Gain% = 8124/32496 * 100 = 25%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A man sells a mobile phone for &#8377;680 and loses something. If he had sold it for &#8377;1070, his gain would have been double the former loss. The cost price (in &#8377;) of the mobile phone is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2342;&#2350;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2379;&#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354; &#2347;&#2379;&#2344; 680 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2360;&#2366;&#2344; &#2313;&#2336;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2327;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; 1070 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2360;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366;&#2404; &#2350;&#2379;&#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354; &#2347;&#2379;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; (&#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["820", "800", "830", "810"], "options_hi": ["820", "800", "830", "810"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the loss be &#8377;X.</p><p>Selling price = &#8377;680</p><p>Cost price = 680 + X</p><p>New selling price = &#8377;1070</p><p>Profit = 2X</p><p>Cost price = 1070  -  2X</p><p>Now, </p><p>680 + X = 1070  -  2X</p><p>3X = 390</p><p>X = 130</p><p>Cost price of the mobile phone = 680 + 130 = &#8377;810</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the loss be &#8377;X.</p><p>Selling price = &#8377;680</p><p>Cost price = 680 + X</p><p>New selling price = &#8377;1070</p><p>Profit = 2X</p><p>Cost price = 1070  -  2X</p><p>Now, </p><p>680 + X = 1070  -  2X</p><p>3X = 390</p><p>X = 130</p><p>Cost price of the mobile phone = 680 + 130 = &#8377;810</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}]}